{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/517816-single-player-campaign","id":517816,"title":"Single player campaign","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-18T04:49:48-07:00","id":517816,"title":"Single player campaign","content":"I'm planning to ST a single player adventure for my wife. So far the only thing I have determined is that it'll be the new World of Darkness, but no particular game line has been chosen. After pondering about it for a couple of days, I figured that Mummy might be an excellent pick. Here's the problem, though - I haven't actually read the book. I participated in the kickstarter, got way too excited at all the previews, then just sifted through the book. For the life of me I have no idea what subsequently distracted me. Probably another RPG. I am known to sometimes have an attention span of a rabbit with ADHD.<br /> <br /> So, of course, I took the book off the shelf and started reading it properly, cover to cover. But that'll probably take a week or two (I'm actually preparing a Spirit of the Century campaign at the same time... ADHD rabbit, as I said...) so in the meantime I just thought I'd ask you wonderful people if you think a single player Mummy campaign would work well. I mean, I know I can make anything work but there are also games where a lot is lost if you don't have a group (Geist, Werewolf, Vampire to an extent...). Would Mummy be a game from that category? And, does anyone actually have any experience with single player Mummy campaigns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T06:44:20-07:00","id":517927,"title":"","content":"Mummies come with their own supporting cast of NPCs to begin with in the form of their Cults, and are generally pretty solitary to begin with. So you won't lose out on much at all by doing single player.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T09:49:47-07:00","id":518255,"title":"","content":"That's exactly the answer I was hoping for. Thanks so much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T10:53:18-07:00","id":518303,"title":"","content":"I ran single Mummy for a long time. It was actually quite lovely, since every flashback could be personalized. Oddly, the player ended up preferring to RP as the heir to the high priest over roping their Mummy. With a Mummy's power level, and the way Memory plays out, it becomes a very engrossing game. You will find its impossible to run out of new material--every supplement so far has been a lot of fun, and each level of memory can introduce new storylines from all across time. With my PC, he woke up in a unique, God-Machine designed tomb, and the Mummy was arisen to find his wife. I kept playing out flashbacks of his prior descent as he got closer on his tail. By the time he finally &quot;rescued&quot; her, he remembered that she was an Angel designed to be a wife for him, and was the one that killed him in his prior life for rebelling against the GM. She was ordered to kill him again, and to store the body permanently in a protected vault--instead, she chose to disobey and Fell. Now, a story like that ccould've been much harder with a group of PCs, but with just the one, it was a great opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T16:22:31-07:00","id":518564,"title":"","content":"I am running single-player Mummy currently.<br /> It's great. Makes the scenes in Neter-Kheret really fun and personal too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T03:08:13-07:00","id":519184,"title":"","content":"Single PC <b>Mummy</b> is how I run it, too. It made it easier to kind of mimic and explore-the-repercussions of The Mummy films; like someone said above, she was resurrected and then prodded to find her reincarnated husband.<br /> <br /> I hope to run a game of Deceived for a group I'm trying to put together with co-workers, though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T05:29:43-07:00","id":519442,"title":"","content":"And now I'm totally stoked to get this started as soon as I'm able to. Thanks, everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T10:33:07-07:00","id":519711,"title":"","content":"Feel free to PM me if you have any other questions ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions"